title: The Statement of 13 March
subtitle: Our first-day statement is being quoted against us on every picket line.
view-if: crisis_kapp = 1 and kapp_statement = 1 and e20_kapp_recanted = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; e20_kapp_recanted = 1
frequency: 150
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= The Statement of 13 March

"The working class will not lift a finger for the democratic republic." The words were the Zentrale's, written in a back room on the first morning. Our members have struck anyway, and they are ashamed of them. [? if comrade_levi = 2 : From his cell Levi has sent out a letter calling the statement a crime against the party. ?]

- @recant: Withdraw it in print, and say plainly that it was wrong.
- @levi: Print Levi's letter, and let him say it for us.
- @stand: Stand by it: this is not our republic.

@recant
subtitle: Our people can hold their heads up on the strike committees again. The Left will say we lost our nerve.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_kapp_voice = 1;
Q.unity -= 4;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 6;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Our voice in the strike: heard';
!}

The Zentrale's second statement appears on the 14th: the party calls on every member to join the general strike.

@levi
subtitle: The strikers will listen to Levi. The Zentrale will look as if it needs a prisoner to think for it.
view-if: comrade_levi = 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_kapp_voice = 1;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 8;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Our voice in the strike: heard';
!}

@stand
subtitle: The Left will be pleased. The party will have no say in what comes after Kapp.
on-arrival: offensive_satisfaction += 6; worker_support -= 3; lean_offensive += 1
